  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>The Glass Cook is a Maine medical cannabis dispensary operating in Fryeburg since 2018. The operator is one of the most distinctive medical dispensaries in Maine, combining three businesses in one location: a licensed medical cannabis dispensary, an on-site glassblowing studio, and a cannabis kitchen called Cured that produces artisanal edibles.</p>
    <p>For medical patients who want more than a transaction — who want to engage with the craft of cannabis culture and the Maine glassblowing tradition — The Glass Cook is a destination. The on-site glassblowing demonstration makes a stop there an experience, not just a dispensary visit.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Three Businesses in One</h2>
    <p><strong>1. Medical cannabis dispensary.</strong> The Glass Cook holds a Maine medical cannabis license. The dispensary carries a full medical menu: flower, pre-rolls, vapes, concentrates, edibles, and CBD products. Maine MMMP card required for cannabis purchases.</p>
    <p><strong>2. On-site glassblowing studio.</strong> The Glass Cook has an active glassblowing studio. Customers can watch glass being made, browse stock pieces, and commission custom work. Per the operator's Yelp listing, "customs orders available. If u need it I can make it."</p>
    <p><strong>3. Cured cannabis kitchen.</strong> The on-site kitchen Cured produces artisanal edibles — gummies, chocolates, baked goods — that are sold through the dispensary. The on-site production kitchen is unusual among Maine medical dispensaries and is part of what differentiates The Glass Cook.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Location and Access</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 295 Bridgton Road, Fryeburg, ME 04037<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 890-8871<br>
    <strong>Hours (per public listings, verify):</strong> Tuesday-Saturday 11am-7pm, closed Sunday and Monday</p>
    <p>Bridgton Road is the main east-west route from Fryeburg to Bridgton — Route 302. The storefront is between downtown Fryeburg and the neighboring town of Bridgton, with easy access from both. Parking is on-site. The glassblowing studio is visible from the parking area, which adds to the destination experience.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>The Glass Cook primarily serves the western Maine and southern New Hampshire medical corridor:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fryeburg</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Bridgton</strong> — 10-15 min east</li>
      <li><strong>Conway / North Conway, NH</strong> — 20-25 min south (NH medical patients)</li>
      <li><strong>Brownfield / Denmark</strong> — 10-15 min</li>
      <li><strong>Lovell / Stow</strong> — 15-20 min</li>
      <li><strong>Cornish / Hiram</strong> — 15-20 min</li>
      <li><strong>Stow / Lovell</strong> — 15-20 min</li>
    </ul>
    <p>New Hampshire residents with a valid Maine MMMP card (or a reciprocity state card) can purchase medical cannabis at The Glass Cook. The operator's glassblowing studio draws visitors from a wider geographic area for both the cannabis and the glassware.</p>
  </section>

